1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,686
Hello, we're Two Tokens One Brain.

2
00:00:02,726 --> 00:00:09,560
Let me show you how Architecture Governance Copilot helps
teams prepare and follow up on architecture reviews.

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:14,309
Today, a project team writes its Solution Intent in Confluence,

4
00:00:14,349 --> 00:00:19,168
tracks the review in Azure Boards,
and discusses the design in Teams.

5
00:00:19,208 --> 00:00:24,363
Afterwards, someone has to bring the decisions,
evidence and action owners back together.

6
00:00:24,403 --> 00:00:27,560
That's the work we're trying to make easier.

7
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,095
Our app helps with drafting and review,

8
00:00:31,135 --> 00:00:35,549
but Confluence remains the source
of truth for the Solution Intent.

9
00:00:35,589 --> 00:00:41,385
We only produce drafts and suggested
changes. The app never edits Confluence.

10
00:00:41,425 --> 00:00:46,249
Users decide what to keep and make those changes themselves.

11
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:54,641
Both project teams and Domain Architects use the
app, with different permissions and responsibilities.

12
00:00:54,681 --> 00:01:00,244
The interface sits in Service Bench.
SKE hosts the backend and database,

13
00:01:00,284 --> 00:01:04,447
with adapters for Confluence, AI Factory and Azure DevOps.

14
00:01:04,487 --> 00:01:10,560
Teams transcripts are imported manually.
Logs, traces and metrics go to COP.

15
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:16,560
Let's start with the project team. I open the project context,

16
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:21,378
which brings together the template,
repository revision and governance details.

17
00:01:21,418 --> 00:01:28,034
I save the supporting evidence, confirm the
package, and generate a Solution Intent draft.

18
00:01:28,074 --> 00:01:30,702
I review and confirm that draft here.

19
00:01:30,742 --> 00:01:34,893
I would then make any changes I want in Confluence myself.

20
00:01:34,933 --> 00:01:37,560
The governance review is a separate step.

21
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:42,684
For the review, I select the authoritative Solution Intent,

22
00:01:42,724 --> 00:01:47,108
import the meeting transcript, and load the review details.

23
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:51,218
I check and confirm these inputs before running the analysis.

24
00:01:51,258 --> 00:01:56,560
The app then puts together a proposal,
with evidence for us to inspect.

25
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:01,396
This is where I review what the app has proposed.

26
00:02:01,436 --> 00:02:08,427
The transcript says Riley will document the retry
controls. I'm changing that action's owner to Taylor Kim.

27
00:02:08,467 --> 00:02:13,804
Notice that Riley's original words
stay visible, alongside my change.

28
00:02:13,844 --> 00:02:17,606
I'm also leaving the retention finding out of this record.

29
00:02:17,646 --> 00:02:21,027
That doesn't mean the issue is resolved or approved.

30
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:28,516
The outcome is still Changes Requested. I confirm
my reviewed record before generating the outputs.

31
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:36,876
The change summary shows what I edited and
left out. Let's follow that retry action:

32
00:02:36,916 --> 00:02:44,816
here's Riley's original quote, then Taylor as the owner I
confirmed, followed by the minutes and work-item preview.

33
00:02:44,856 --> 00:02:48,204
We can check how the final action came from

34
00:02:48,244 --> 00:02:51,593
the original discussion, and see where I changed it.

35
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:59,838
Next, I'll deliver the work item. I
preview the request and check the owner,

36
00:02:59,878 --> 00:03:03,127
due date, parent reference and supporting evidence.

37
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:06,309
The summary and JSON show the same request.

38
00:03:06,349 --> 00:03:11,082
Once I'm happy with it, I confirm and create the work item.

39
00:03:11,122 --> 00:03:14,519
The app reads it back to check the result.

40
00:03:14,559 --> 00:03:19,482
The receipt is visible here, and this
action can't simply be submitted again.

41
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:26,466
Now let's see what happens if I change the transcript.

42
00:03:26,506 --> 00:03:31,093
I add some new context, and the previous outputs become invalid.

43
00:03:31,133 --> 00:03:36,221
I need to run the analysis and review
again before using new outputs.

44
00:03:36,261 --> 00:03:39,771
The work item I already delivered is still recorded.

45
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:44,736
We've made edits easier to see, evidence easier to follow,

46
00:03:44,776 --> 00:03:48,560
and delivery easier to check. That's our response to the feedback.

47
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:54,165
That's our demo. We want teams to spend
less time piecing reviews together,

48
00:03:54,205 --> 00:03:57,560
while keeping people in control. Thank you for watching.
